<title>UK: Reuters 5th ex-UK-Americas air cargo market report.</title>
<headline>Reuters 5th ex-UK-Americas air cargo market report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK air cargo rates to the United States per kg for a 100 kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one.</p>
<p>		   April 11		March 27</p>
<p>		  UNITED STATES</p>
<p> LON-CHI	   0.74		   0.74</p>
<p> LON-JFK	   0.62		   0.62</p>
<p> LON-LAX	   0.77		   0.80</p>
<p>.LON-MIA	   0.63		   0.63</p>
<p>		  LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p> LON-SAO	   1.86		   1.90</p>
<p> LON-BUE	   2.00		   2.02</p>
<p> LON-SCL	   1.84		   1.80</p>
<p> LON-CCS	   1.30		   N.A.</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents at the three main London airports.</p>
<p>*All prices are quoted in sterling.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative of current market activity. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
